      "nets": ["RST", "SDA", "PWM", "SCK"],
      "observed": "The ATtiny45 U2 and ATtiny13 U3 have corresponding reset and GPIO pins directly connected to the same nets. For example, both PB1 pins are on PWM and both PB2 pins are on SCK. Their VCC and GND pins are also shared.",
      "expected": "A board should use one active MCU for these shared signals, or clearly define the two MCU footprints as mutually exclusive assembly alternatives. Independent MCU GPIOs should not be paralleled without isolation or a defined coordination scheme.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"10\") (name \"PWM\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"PB1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"12\") (name \"SCK\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PB2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"11\") (name \"RST\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"~{RESET}/PB5\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"~{RESET}/PB5\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U2\") (value \"ATtiny45-20P\") ... (footprint \"Package_DIP:DIP-8_W7.62mm\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U3\") (value \"ATtiny13V-10S\") ... (footprint \"Package_SO:SOIC-8W_5.3x5.3mm_P1.27mm\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If both footprints are populated, both MCUs can drive shared signals such as PWM and programming lines. Their outputs may contend or behave inconsistently, preventing reliable fan control or programming. The files do not indicate that the two MCU placements are mutually exclusive.",
      "confidence": 0.76
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design connects two different ATtiny devices in parallel across the same supply, reset, and GPIO nets. This is problematic if both are populated; the files do not identify them as mutually exclusive assembly options."
}

